1
00:00:09,250 --> 00:00:10,875
This is Variantly.

2
00:00:10,875 --> 00:00:13,267
In the next ten minutes, I'll show you one

3
00:00:13,267 --> 00:00:15,891
whole run, including what it costs and how

4
00:00:15,891 --> 00:00:16,680
to undo it.

5
00:00:16,680 --> 00:00:20,047
I'm Joaquin, and I built Variantly because

6
00:00:20,047 --> 00:00:22,752
redesigning a site usually means betting

7
00:00:22,752 --> 00:00:24,204
on one direction.

8
00:00:24,204 --> 00:00:26,143
If it's wrong, you start over.

9
00:00:26,143 --> 00:00:29,242
Here, your agent builds several complete

10
00:00:29,242 --> 00:00:31,982
redesigns at once, each one running as

11
00:00:31,982 --> 00:00:34,026
your real site, and you keep the one you

12
00:00:34,026 --> 00:00:34,767
like.

13
00:00:34,767 --> 00:00:37,565
Here's what we'll cover: setting up a run,

14
00:00:37,565 --> 00:00:40,282
giving each variant its own direction,

15
00:00:40,282 --> 00:00:42,569
comparing them on your real site, and

16
00:00:42,569 --> 00:00:43,841
keeping one.

17
00:00:44,333 --> 00:00:45,947
First, the mental model.

18
00:00:45,947 --> 00:00:47,967
Your project stays where it is.

19
00:00:47,967 --> 00:00:50,823
Each variant is its own copy: a git

20
00:00:50,823 --> 00:00:53,366
worktree on its own branch, a little

21
00:00:53,366 --> 00:00:56,106
timeline of your site, with a preview.

22
00:00:56,106 --> 00:00:58,822
You compare them side by side, keep one,

23
00:00:58,822 --> 00:01:01,190
and a last pass rolls it out to the whole

24
00:01:01,190 --> 00:01:01,951
site.

25
00:01:02,433 --> 00:01:05,103
You need two things: Node, and a coding

26
00:01:05,103 --> 00:01:06,851
agent you already use.

27
00:01:07,135 --> 00:01:11,779
In your project folder, run npx variantly,

28
00:01:11,779 --> 00:01:14,577
and a wizard opens in your browser.

29
00:01:14,577 --> 00:01:17,689
The design work is done by Impeccable, an

30
00:01:17,689 --> 00:01:19,871
open-source design skill.

31
00:01:19,871 --> 00:01:22,669
One catch: it has to be the command-line

32
00:01:22,669 --> 00:01:25,282
agent, not a browser builder like Lovable

33
00:01:25,282 --> 00:01:26,321
or Bolt.

34
00:01:26,817 --> 00:01:28,338
Will it work on yours?

35
00:01:28,338 --> 00:01:31,670
Here's variantly doctor on a Next.js app,

36
00:01:31,670 --> 00:01:35,002
a Django site, and plain HTML.

37
00:01:35,002 --> 00:01:37,521
It finds the stack, and the command that

38
00:01:37,521 --> 00:01:38,857
serves it, every time.

39
00:01:38,857 --> 00:01:41,138
And you can always type your own.

40
00:01:41,633 --> 00:01:44,176
Here's a rough edge, on purpose.

41
00:01:44,176 --> 00:01:47,032
This folder has no commit yet, so doctor

42
00:01:47,032 --> 00:01:48,808
marks it with a cross.

43
00:01:48,808 --> 00:01:51,293
Variantly can make that first commit for

44
00:01:51,293 --> 00:01:54,933
you, or you fix it and run doctor again.

45
00:01:55,433 --> 00:01:56,687
Not a developer?

46
00:01:56,687 --> 00:01:59,450
If you can paste a command, you're set.

47
00:01:59,450 --> 00:02:01,668
On variantly.style, there's a

48
00:02:01,668 --> 00:02:02,921
walk-me-through prompt.

49
00:02:02,921 --> 00:02:05,603
Paste it into any AI chat, and it takes

50
00:02:05,603 --> 00:02:08,500
you through it one small step at a time.

51
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:14,532
Setup finds your app and checks your

52
00:02:14,532 --> 00:02:15,217
agent.

53
00:02:15,217 --> 00:02:17,980
Each card says if it's ready, and if not,

54
00:02:17,980 --> 00:02:20,041
the fix is right on the card.

55
00:02:20,197 --> 00:02:21,904
I'm using Claude Code.

56
00:02:21,904 --> 00:02:24,923
You could pick Codex, Copilot, Gemini,

57
00:02:24,923 --> 00:02:29,149
Cursor, OpenCode, Grok Build, Antigravity,

58
00:02:29,149 --> 00:02:32,702
Pi, Hermes Agent, or any OpenRouter model,

59
00:02:32,702 --> 00:02:34,763
and mix them in one run.

60
00:02:35,250 --> 00:02:36,423
Why mix them?

61
00:02:36,423 --> 00:02:39,766
Each model has its own design instincts.

62
00:02:39,766 --> 00:02:42,680
So you get more varied directions, you see

63
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:45,653
which model designs best for your site,

64
00:02:45,653 --> 00:02:47,858
and you spread the work across accounts

65
00:02:47,858 --> 00:02:49,391
you already pay for.

66
00:02:49,391 --> 00:02:52,119
Add --blind, and you won't see who made

67
00:02:52,119 --> 00:02:54,308
each one until you've kept it.

68
00:02:54,783 --> 00:02:56,176
Next, what to make.

69
00:02:56,176 --> 00:02:59,323
The quick picks are two, four or six.

70
00:02:59,323 --> 00:03:01,923
I'll pick six, then step it up to ten

71
00:03:01,923 --> 00:03:05,174
under More settings, with five agents at a

72
00:03:05,174 --> 00:03:07,368
time, so it runs in two waves.

73
00:03:07,368 --> 00:03:09,644
The rarer settings stay back there.

74
00:03:09,644 --> 00:03:12,117
That's progressive disclosure: the common

75
00:03:12,117 --> 00:03:13,888
path stays short.

76
00:03:15,833 --> 00:03:17,331
Now, your own directions.

77
00:03:17,331 --> 00:03:19,804
Every slot starts blank, and blank means

78
00:03:19,804 --> 00:03:21,046
Impeccable picks.

79
00:03:21,046 --> 00:03:23,647
To pin one, type it in your own words.

80
00:03:23,647 --> 00:03:26,061
Tactile imperfection: raw paper,

81
00:03:26,061 --> 00:03:27,535
brushstrokes, stitching.

82
00:03:27,535 --> 00:03:29,602
Surreal distortion: impossible

83
00:03:29,602 --> 00:03:31,686
proportions, dreamlike light.

84
00:03:31,843 --> 00:03:33,758
These are the trends I'm watching this

85
00:03:33,758 --> 00:03:36,823
winter: human-made texture meeting digital

86
00:03:36,823 --> 00:03:38,101
surrealism.

87
00:03:38,101 --> 00:03:40,690
One per variant, and any slot you leave

88
00:03:40,690 --> 00:03:43,111
blank, Impeccable picks.

89
00:04:00,783 --> 00:04:03,639
A few words about your site, and what must

90
00:04:03,639 --> 00:04:07,354
stay: here, the prices, the sign-up button

91
00:04:07,354 --> 00:04:08,956
and the FAQ.

92
00:04:08,956 --> 00:04:10,222
Then the review.

93
00:04:10,222 --> 00:04:12,486
I designed this screen to show exactly

94
00:04:12,486 --> 00:04:14,790
what will run, and what it costs.

95
00:04:14,947 --> 00:04:18,337
Variantly is free and open source; each

96
00:04:18,337 --> 00:04:21,495
variant is one session on your own plan,

97
00:04:21,495 --> 00:04:23,573
plus one for its review.

98
00:04:23,573 --> 00:04:26,092
Ten variants, twenty sessions.

99
00:04:26,092 --> 00:04:27,288
Trying it out?

100
00:04:27,288 --> 00:04:28,896
Start with four.

101
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:31,281
Can this break your site?

102
00:04:31,281 --> 00:04:31,850
No.

103
00:04:31,850 --> 00:04:34,636
Each variant runs in an isolated git

104
00:04:34,636 --> 00:04:36,946
worktree, outside your project, so your

105
00:04:36,946 --> 00:04:38,938
main branch is never touched.

106
00:04:39,152 --> 00:04:41,683
And agents change presentation, never

107
00:04:41,683 --> 00:04:42,618
behaviour.

108
00:04:42,774 --> 00:04:46,002
Ten worktrees, ten dev servers, five

109
00:04:46,002 --> 00:04:47,854
agents at a time.

110
00:04:48,333 --> 00:04:51,119
The board shows each variant's direction,

111
00:04:51,119 --> 00:04:53,383
progress and time, live.

112
00:04:53,383 --> 00:04:54,811
Let's follow one.

113
00:04:54,811 --> 00:04:57,238
It reads your site, builds its direction,

114
00:04:57,238 --> 00:04:59,873
then opens it in a real browser, at

115
00:04:59,873 --> 00:05:02,706
desktop and phone width, and fixes what it

116
00:05:02,706 --> 00:05:03,507
sees.

117
00:05:03,507 --> 00:05:06,271
A second pass critiques and audits it,

118
00:05:06,271 --> 00:05:08,320
keeping the direction.

119
00:05:08,817 --> 00:05:11,696
Real time, for the record: the whole run

120
00:05:11,696 --> 00:05:15,028
took about 60 minutes, start to finish, so

121
00:05:15,028 --> 00:05:17,194
here's the rest, sped up.

122
00:05:17,417 --> 00:05:20,761
If a variant fails, the board says why, in

123
00:05:20,761 --> 00:05:23,675
the agent's own words, and you retry just

124
00:05:23,675 --> 00:05:24,668
that one.

125
00:05:24,824 --> 00:05:28,005
And if one comes out broken, like a layout

126
00:05:28,005 --> 00:05:30,838
that falls apart on a phone, tell the

127
00:05:30,838 --> 00:05:33,717
agent to fix it, retry it, or just don't

128
00:05:33,717 --> 00:05:34,710
keep it.

129
00:05:35,200 --> 00:05:36,257
Then, compare.

130
00:05:36,257 --> 00:05:38,161
This is your real site running, not

131
00:05:38,161 --> 00:05:40,192
screenshots, so you're judging the real

132
00:05:40,192 --> 00:05:42,584
thing: real type, real layout, real

133
00:05:42,584 --> 00:05:43,582
interactions.

134
00:05:43,582 --> 00:05:46,583
Drag the divider for a before and after.

135
00:05:46,583 --> 00:05:50,054
One: tactile imperfection, paper grain and

136
00:05:50,054 --> 00:05:51,355
stitched rules.

137
00:05:51,355 --> 00:05:54,733
Two: surreal distortion, cold light and

138
00:05:54,733 --> 00:05:56,266
impossible scale.

139
00:05:56,266 --> 00:05:59,261
Three: cinematic drama, deep shadow and

140
00:05:59,261 --> 00:06:00,254
oxblood.

141
00:06:00,399 --> 00:06:03,661
Four: maximalist collage, cut-outs that

142
00:06:03,661 --> 00:06:04,520
still read.

143
00:06:04,520 --> 00:06:07,411
Five: retro-tech, an early desktop with

144
00:06:07,411 --> 00:06:08,618
modern type.

145
00:06:08,618 --> 00:06:11,486
Six: expressive typography, where the type

146
00:06:11,486 --> 00:06:12,723
is the event.

147
00:06:12,937 --> 00:06:15,863
Seven: warm eclecticism, wood and mixed

148
00:06:15,863 --> 00:06:16,728
eras.

149
00:06:16,943 --> 00:06:19,392
Eight: neo-folk craft, one named

150
00:06:19,392 --> 00:06:20,432
tradition.

151
00:06:20,646 --> 00:06:23,183
Nine: soft chrome and glass.

152
00:06:23,339 --> 00:06:26,846
Ten: quiet organic minimalism, space and

153
00:06:26,846 --> 00:06:28,025
earth tones.

154
00:06:28,239 --> 00:06:30,909
S puts them side by side, both panes

155
00:06:30,909 --> 00:06:33,191
labelled, on one scrollbar.

156
00:06:33,347 --> 00:06:35,455
M is the phone layout.

157
00:06:35,967 --> 00:06:37,941
Or press L for the lens.

158
00:06:37,941 --> 00:06:40,321
One design fills the screen, and the next

159
00:06:40,321 --> 00:06:42,724
one shows through a door that follows your

160
00:06:42,724 --> 00:06:43,455
mouse.

161
00:06:43,455 --> 00:06:45,969
Click, and you keep the one in the door.

162
00:06:46,733 --> 00:06:49,299
Pause the video for a moment, and think:

163
00:06:49,299 --> 00:06:51,505
which of these ten would you keep for your

164
00:06:51,505 --> 00:06:52,649
own site?

165
00:06:58,133 --> 00:06:59,747
Here's how I decide.

166
00:06:59,747 --> 00:07:02,185
First, does it still read clearly?

167
00:07:02,185 --> 00:07:04,600
Second, does it fit the people who use the

168
00:07:04,600 --> 00:07:05,029
site?

169
00:07:05,029 --> 00:07:07,607
And third, would it hold up on every other

170
00:07:07,607 --> 00:07:08,234
page?

171
00:07:08,234 --> 00:07:11,665
Today, I'm keeping tactile imperfection.

172
00:07:12,150 --> 00:07:14,669
Every variant is scored against your

173
00:07:14,669 --> 00:07:17,049
original, right on your machine, with

174
00:07:17,049 --> 00:07:18,582
axe-core and Lighthouse.

175
00:07:18,582 --> 00:07:20,741
You only see the change: how many

176
00:07:20,741 --> 00:07:23,365
accessibility points it gained, and how

177
00:07:23,365 --> 00:07:25,490
many axe issues it fixed.

178
00:07:25,490 --> 00:07:27,957
So it's evidence, not just a look.

179
00:07:28,450 --> 00:07:30,203
And if you hate all ten?

180
00:07:30,203 --> 00:07:32,281
Run it again with a sharper brief.

181
00:07:32,281 --> 00:07:34,940
Nothing is kept unless you press Keep, and

182
00:07:34,940 --> 00:07:38,887
npx variantly clean removes every worktree

183
00:07:38,887 --> 00:07:40,264
and branch it made.

184
00:07:40,750 --> 00:07:42,155
Keep the one you like.

185
00:07:42,155 --> 00:07:45,092
Notice this checkbox: one last agent pass

186
00:07:45,092 --> 00:07:47,379
carries the look to every other page.

187
00:07:47,379 --> 00:07:49,307
That's why we only previewed the home

188
00:07:49,307 --> 00:07:49,957
page.

189
00:07:49,957 --> 00:07:52,139
You judge one page, and the rest of the

190
00:07:52,139 --> 00:07:53,539
site follows.

191
00:07:59,717 --> 00:08:02,202
It lands in your working tree, merged with

192
00:08:02,202 --> 00:08:04,112
anything you've changed since.

193
00:08:04,268 --> 00:08:07,089
The last commit is still yours: nothing is

194
00:08:07,089 --> 00:08:07,943
committed.

195
00:08:08,099 --> 00:08:10,572
So you review it like any other change,

196
00:08:10,572 --> 00:08:12,500
and undo it the same way.

197
00:08:12,500 --> 00:08:15,263
You keep one timeline; the others stay as

198
00:08:15,263 --> 00:08:18,595
branches until you run npx variantly

199
00:08:18,595 --> 00:08:19,658
clean.

200
00:08:20,150 --> 00:08:22,379
Then hand off to your own agent.

201
00:08:22,379 --> 00:08:24,771
Open your site, and this prompt gives it

202
00:08:24,771 --> 00:08:27,116
the local address, the design notes, and

203
00:08:27,116 --> 00:08:28,434
what to check.

204
00:08:38,767 --> 00:08:41,635
The website got the same care: twenty

205
00:08:41,635 --> 00:08:44,735
title concepts, thirty redesigns of one

206
00:08:44,735 --> 00:08:47,776
shop, and a mobile pass that cut its

207
00:08:47,776 --> 00:08:50,807
transfer, font requests and blocking time

208
00:08:50,807 --> 00:08:52,299
on phones.

209
00:09:07,367 --> 00:09:10,444
To recap: each variant is an isolated

210
00:09:10,444 --> 00:09:13,044
copy, its own branch of your site.

211
00:09:13,044 --> 00:09:15,529
You can pin a direction per variant, and

212
00:09:15,529 --> 00:09:16,934
mix agents.

213
00:09:16,934 --> 00:09:19,407
You compare on your real site, with real

214
00:09:19,407 --> 00:09:20,196
scores.

215
00:09:20,196 --> 00:09:22,204
And you keep one, and it rolls out

216
00:09:22,204 --> 00:09:23,267
site-wide.

217
00:09:23,767 --> 00:09:26,669
I designed and directed Variantly with

218
00:09:26,669 --> 00:09:29,293
Claude Code and Impeccable: I set the

219
00:09:29,293 --> 00:09:32,045
direction, made the calls, and tested it

220
00:09:32,045 --> 00:09:33,357
on a real iPhone.

221
00:09:33,357 --> 00:09:35,946
It's free and open source, and it runs on

222
00:09:35,946 --> 00:09:36,910
your machine.

223
00:09:36,910 --> 00:09:39,278
No account, no server of ours.

224
00:09:39,278 --> 00:09:42,912
To try it, run npx variantly in your

225
00:09:42,912 --> 00:09:43,760
project.

226
00:09:43,760 --> 00:09:46,140
Docs at variantly.style.

227
00:09:46,140 --> 00:09:47,748
Thanks for watching.
